; user-hop tests (see test.md). Run from B> in user 0; needs the user-4 files
T Hop test
E@4  Hop: DIR in user 4          | DIR U4MARK.*
EP@4 Hop, pause                  | DIR U4MARK.*
E!@4 Hop, leave to the prompt    | DIR U4MARK.*
S@4  Hop with an S file          | HOPS
SP@4 Hop with an S file, pause   | HOPS
S!@4 Hop with an S file, leave   | HOPS
E@4  Program only in user 4      | HELLO
E@4  Nested: menu in user 4      | B:MENU B:HOP4.DAT
E@0  Same user as home: no hop   | DIR U0MARK.*
E@15 Hop to user 15             | DIR
E@4  Missing program in user 4  | NOSUCH
E   Plain entry, no hop         | DIR U0MARK.*
